Subject: [PATCH] build(cmake): link system zlib for IWorkFile on macOS

Apple/IWorkFile compiles zlib_addon.c (which calls inflate/inflateEnd/
inflateInit2_) but does not build zlib itself; it relies on the linked kernel
library re-exporting those zlib symbols. On macOS (Mach-O two-level namespace +
-fvisibility=hidden) kernel does not re-export them, so the IWorkFile link fails
with undefined zlib symbols. Link the system zlib directly on Apple.

---

diff --git a/Apple/CMakeLists.txt b/Apple/CMakeLists.txt
index 5a16948f1..a493600fb 100644
--- a/Apple/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/Apple/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -469,6 +469,15 @@ target_link_libraries(IWorkFile PUBLIC
     UnicodeConverter
 )
 
+if(APPLE)
+    # IWorkFile compiles zlib_addon.c (inflate/inflateEnd/inflateInit2_) but not
+    # zlib itself, relying on kernel re-exporting those symbols. With Mach-O's
+    # two-level namespace + hidden visibility kernel does not re-export them, so
+    # link the system zlib directly.
+    find_package(ZLIB REQUIRED)
+    target_link_libraries(IWorkFile PRIVATE ZLIB::ZLIB)
+endif()
+
 copy_artifacts_to_folder("IWorkFile" "${EO_CORE_OUTPUT_DIR}")
 
 declare_victory( IWorkFile )
